From 46e66636cebe4958e36a996a21b6c50e784f679b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:38:24 +0100
Subject: mips: Match the Linux sigaction ABI

Linux on MIPS uses a kernel-provided signal return trampoline, and its
sigaction structure ends with the signal mask. Since Linux 5.11 the
kernel clears the obsolete SA_RESTORER bit. Valgrind expected that bit
back in its host signal action, causing logread to abort when changing
the SIGPIPE disposition. The guest wrapper also read and wrote an
extra restorer pointer past the end of the kernel structure.

Use the Linux layout for host and guest actions on MIPS32 and MIPS64.
Leave the host restorer to the kernel and use Valgrind's existing
trampolines when delivering guest signals. For the legacy MIPS32
syscall, read only the first input mask word and zero the upper words
in the result, as the kernel does.

Add a regression test for querying actions without modifying adjacent
data, legacy mask conversion, and signal delivery. Verified on
big-endian MIPS32 OpenWrt and little-endian MIPS64 Linux.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
